OK   the table has 20 transitions and 8 non-halting states
OK   decides {w#w}: on all 88573 inputs over {0,1,#} of length <= 10 it accepts exactly the members and rejects the rest (never crashes, never runs on)  [{'reject': 88542, 'accept': 31}]
OK   on every input of length n <= 10 it halts within 2n^2 + 3n + 2 steps (the bound in (d))  [{0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 3, 3: 8, 4: 11, 5: 18, 6: 23, 7: 32, 8: 39, 9: 50, 10: 59}]
OK   exact count: on w#w with |w| = k it takes 2(k+1)^2 steps, for every w with k <= 7
OK   even lengths: on w#w0 (n = 2k + 2) it rejects after 2(k+1)^2 = n^2/2 steps, for every w with k <= 7
